@* Covers the viewport while the model is being worked out.

   It names the step that is running rather than guessing at a percentage. The
   steps are not equal shares of the work - which one dominates depends on the
   model - so a bar filling smoothly would be a fiction. What the user needs to
   know is that something is happening and roughly how far along it is. *@

@if (Visible)
{
    <div class="working" role="status" aria-live="polite">
        <div class="working-card">
            <div class="working-spinner" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <div class="working-text">
                <strong>@Message</strong>
                @if (Steps > 0)
                {
                    <span class="working-step">Schritt @Step von @Steps</span>
                    <progress class="working-bar" max="@Steps" value="@Finished"></progress>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
}
